1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,100
Alright, Barnsley Town!

2
00:00:02,520 --> 00:00:05,200
Chambers on the corner, Bhramahs in the air

3
00:00:05,680 --> 00:00:09,200
Creepy Steve’s by the bins like he’s always been there

4
00:00:09,980 --> 00:00:12,280
Council flat kingdom, kettle on the boil

5
00:00:12,320 --> 00:00:14,700
Lift smells funny but we’re loyal to the soil

6
00:00:15,020 --> 00:00:16,800
Mucky woman’s laughing in a dressing gown

7
00:00:16,800 --> 00:00:19,080
Says, “I’ve got class, love” — then she falls straight down

8
00:00:19,080 --> 00:00:21,960
Creepy Steve’s got a raincoat and a plastic cup

9
00:00:21,960 --> 00:00:24,200
Knows every back door, every shortcut up

10
00:00:24,620 --> 00:00:26,240
Bhramahs on the table, crisps in a bowl

11
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:28,210
Weed in the garden, keeping slugs on patrol

12
00:00:28,260 --> 00:00:30,560
If the rent’s gone up, we’ll blame the moon

13
00:00:30,600 --> 00:00:32,720
If the telly breaks, we’ll fix it with a spoon

14
00:00:32,920 --> 00:00:35,280
From the stairwell choir to the busted old van

15
00:00:35,320 --> 00:00:38,060
We’re making do, mate — that’s the council plan

16
00:00:38,360 --> 00:00:40,440
Crazy cuz, crazy cuz, what you playing at?

17
00:00:40,480 --> 00:00:42,720
Mucky woman’s moonwalking in a leopard hat

18
00:00:42,760 --> 00:00:45,000
Barnsley Town, sing it loud, don’t be shy

19
00:00:45,200 --> 00:00:47,320
Chambers pub calling, so we’re giving it a try

20
00:00:47,540 --> 00:00:49,800
Crazy cuz, crazy cuz, life’s a funny little tune

21
00:00:50,440 --> 00:00:51,920
Bhramahs, bits of weed, and a washing line balloon

22
00:00:51,960 --> 00:00:53,960
Creepy Steve says, “One more?” — and we all shout, “Course!”

23
00:00:54,000 --> 00:00:57,500
Then we lose the last bus crawling back from Chambers!

24
00:01:02,220 --> 00:01:07,420
The hallway’s got a mystery stain with history

25
00:01:07,800 --> 00:01:10,000
Landlord calls it “character,” we call it misery

26
00:01:10,400 --> 00:01:12,560
Mucky woman’s got a handbag full of receipts

27
00:01:12,560 --> 00:01:15,000
And a kebab that’s been ageing for three weeks

28
00:01:15,040 --> 00:01:17,300
Creepy Steve’s doing parkour by the bin store

29
00:01:17,560 --> 00:01:19,600
Missed the landing, now he’s knocking on floor four

30
00:01:19,980 --> 00:01:21,900
Bhramahs makes the wisdom seem surprisingly deep

31
00:01:22,140 --> 00:01:24,100
“Never trust a pigeon that refuses to sleep”

32
00:01:24,320 --> 00:01:26,740
The neighbour’s got a barbecue made from a chair

33
00:01:26,740 --> 00:01:28,740
Someone’s growing herbs in the communal air

34
00:01:28,780 --> 00:01:31,220
We’ve got big dreams and a tiny front room

35
00:01:31,260 --> 00:01:33,500
But the bass through the ceiling makes the whole block boom

36
00:01:33,780 --> 00:01:35,900
Crazy cuz, crazy cuz, what you playing at?

37
00:01:36,080 --> 00:01:38,200
Mucky woman’s moonwalking in a leopard hat

38
00:01:38,400 --> 00:01:40,620
Barnsley Town, sing it loud, don’t be shy

39
00:01:40,620 --> 00:01:42,800
Chambers pub calling, so we’re giving it a try

40
00:01:43,000 --> 00:01:45,300
Crazy cuz, crazy cuz, life’s a funny little tune

41
00:01:45,580 --> 00:01:47,300
Bhramahs, bits of weed, and a washing line balloon

42
00:01:47,340 --> 00:01:49,400
Creepy Steve says, “One more?” — and we all shout, “Course!”

43
00:01:49,440 --> 00:01:52,500
Then we lose the last bus crawling back from Chambers!

44
00:01:52,600 --> 00:02:06,500
♪ (Da-ba-dee, da-ba-da, da-ba-dee, da-ba-da...) ♪

45
00:02:06,600 --> 00:02:21,500
♪ (Da-ba-dee, da-ba-da, da-ba-dee, da-ba-da!) ♪

46
00:02:22,360 --> 00:02:24,200
Crazy cuz, crazy cuz, clap along with that

47
00:02:24,200 --> 00:02:26,460
Mucky woman’s singing through a borrowed megaphone hat

48
00:02:26,600 --> 00:02:28,760
Barnsley Town, raise the roof, let it fly

49
00:02:28,760 --> 00:02:31,200
We’re too skint for taxis but we still get by

50
00:02:31,460 --> 00:02:33,660
Crazy cuz, crazy cuz, laughing at the doom

51
00:02:33,660 --> 00:02:35,720
Weed by the window, Bhramahs in the room

52
00:02:35,840 --> 00:02:38,180
Creepy Steve says, “Last one!” — we all know the score

53
00:02:38,180 --> 00:02:41,320
Then we’re dancing in the drizzle outside Chambers’ door!

54
00:02:41,320 --> 00:02:43,580
Barnsley Town, council crown

55
00:02:43,580 --> 00:02:45,640
Creepy Steve, don’t let us down

56
00:02:45,860 --> 00:02:48,240
Bhramahs, weed, and a night outdoors

57
00:02:48,240 --> 00:02:51,160
See you next week, same time, same Chambers!

58
00:02:51,200 --> 00:03:00,680
♪ Chambers... Chambers! ♪
